# OpenDiscourse Windsurf Rules
# This file guides the AI assistant in generating code that adheres to our standards

# Core Rules
- Always follow PEP 8 style guide
- Use type hints for all function parameters and return values
- Document all public APIs with Google-style docstrings
- Include comprehensive error handling
- Write unit tests for new functionality

# File Structure
- Keep files under 500 lines
- Split large files into smaller modules
- Use `__init__.py` to define public API

# Import Order
1. Standard library imports
2. Third-party imports
3. Local application imports

# Type Hints
- Use Python 3.9+ type hints (list[Type], dict[Key, Value])
- Define custom types using TypeVar when needed
- Use Optional[Type] for nullable values

# Error Handling
- Create specific exception classes
- Include context in error messages
- Use try/except blocks judiciously
- Never use bare except clauses

# Documentation
- Document all public APIs
- Include Args, Returns, and Raises in docstrings
- Keep docstrings up-to-date with code changes
- Include examples for complex functions

# Testing
- Write unit tests for all new functionality
- Aim for high test coverage
- Test edge cases and error conditions
- Use fixtures and parameterized tests where appropriate